      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[concepts/credential-scoping]], the Anthropic API key is **injected into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts**. \n\nThe key specifics are:\n\n- A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n- The key is injected only into the environment of the child process (not the Hub\u0027s own process)\n- The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated\n- The same scoping model applies to the Query agent process \u2014 it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn\n\nThis design ensures that a compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the credential by inspecting environment variables, since the key only exists inside the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 5127,
